course: dictionary
lesson: 1964
title: Compete: trying to win
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: To compete means to try to win against others, or to try to be more successful than they are. Look at the words around it to find the clues. «Kieran competes with Sam at everything: who's taller, who runs faster.» The words "with Sam" tell you that two people are trying to beat each other.
explain: Compete often has a small word after it, like compete in, compete against, compete for or compete with. That little word tells you what the contest is about or who you are up against. «Several people usually compete for one job» means each person wants the same job, and only one can have it.
explain: Competing can be fair or unfair. «Competing is fine, but hurting a teammate to win is never fine.» So the word means trying hard against others, but winning by hurting someone is not allowed.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «Kieran tries to beat Sam at everything» still makes sense, so "try to beat" is a good meaning for compete.
fact: «Compete» means to try to win against others, or to try to be more successful than others.
fact: Compete is a verb, so its forms are compete, competes, competed and competing.
fact: In nature, living things compete for food, water, light and space.
fact: Use compete in a race or contest, compete against a rival, compete for a prize or job, and compete with someone for the same thing.
fact: Competing is fine, but hurting someone to win is never fine.
exercise: «Kieran competes with Sam at everything.» What does compete mean here? | *To try to beat someone | To sleep next to someone | To give someone a present | To copy someone's homework
exercise: In nature, what do plants and animals compete for? | Only rainy days | Shoes and socks | Ice cream on Sundays | *Food, water, light and space
exercise: Which little word goes with a race? Say "compete ___ a race." | off | *in | under | across
test: «Lemurs... with no monkeys on the island to compete» gives them a chance to spread out. What does compete mean here? | To count the trees | To travel by boat | *To fight rivals for food and space | To sing beautifully
test: Which way of competing is fair? | Hurting a teammate to win | Cheating in a spelling bee | Tripping up the runner next to you | *Practising hard to beat your own best time
exam: A job interview is a meeting where an employer asks questions. Why do people compete for one job? | Because interviews are always on Sundays | Because nobody wants the job | Because the employer wants a holiday | *Because several people want the same job and only one can get it
